<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">The above results were reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors in their  nmeeting held on June 23, 2020.  nEffective ist April, 2019, the Company has adopted Ind AS 116  Leases  applied to all lease contracts existing  non April 1, 2019 using the modified retrospective method along with the transition option to recognise Rightof-  nUse (ROU) at amount equal to the lease liability. In the Statement of Profit and Loss account, depreciation  non right of use and finance cost for interest accrued on lease liability is being accounted for as against operating  nlease rent included under  Other expenses  earlier. The comparatives for the quarter and year ended March 31,  n2019 have not been retrospectively adjusted. This change did not have a material impact on the financial results  nfor the quarter and year ended March 31, 2020.  nThe Company is in the business of “Power Products” which is a single business segment in accordance with Ind  nAS-108  Operating Segment  notified pursuant to Companies (Accounting Standards) Rule, 2015.  nExceptional items  nExpense:  na) 2018-19 Rs. 350 lakhs represent the amount incurred and paid on account of final settlement in  nrespect of disputed matter related to lease hold land of the company situated at Rudrapur.  nb) 2019-20 - Government of India in Finance (No. 2) Bill, 2019 has introduced Sabka Vishwas (Legacy  nDispute Resolution) Scheme, 2019, which provides an option to settle eligible tax disputes. During the  ncurrent year the Company has decided to avail this option to settle eligible tax disputes amounting to  nRs. 2,196 lakhs and consequently an amount of Rs. 1,086 lakhs has been provided during current year  nfor this purpose.  nIncome: 2019-20 -   nTill 2018-19 the Company was claiming export incentives under Merchandise Exports  nfrom India Scheme (MEIS) on export sales made to a few countries. During the current year based on the  nexport pricing strategy, the Company has decided to claim export incentive on exports made to all  ncountries. The additional export benefits related to the year April 1, 2016 to March 31, 2019 amounting to  nRs. 1,523 lakhs (2016-17 - Rs. 436 lakhs, 2017-18 — Rs. 525 lakhs &amp; 2018-19 — Rs. 562 lakhs) have been  nrecognized during the current year as exceptional income.  nOn 20% September 2019, Government of India vide the Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance 2019, inserted  nSection 115BAA in the Income Tax Act, 1961, which provides domestic companies an option to pay Income Tax  nat reduced rate effective April 1, 2019, subject to certain conditions. The tax expenses for the quarter and year  nended March 31, 2020 have been provided for at reduced tax rate. Accordingly, tax expense is lower and profit  nfor the year ended March 31, 2020 is higher by Rs. 853 lakhs.  nThe figures of the quarters ending March 31, 2019 &amp; March 31, 2020 are the balancing figures between the  naudited figures in respect of the relevant financial years and the published unaudited year to date figures up to  nthe third quarter of the relevant financial years.  nThe Board of Directors have recommended a dividend of Rs. 12:5/- per share (125 % of an equity share of par  nvalue of Rs. 10/- each) for the year ended March 31, 2020. The Payment is subject to approval of the shareholder at the ensuing Annual General Meeting of the Company.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
